<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2022-tame-30--gpt> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on levin-2022-tame-30: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.43";
    dc:description "Existing comparative and perturbation data can test whether homeostasis buffers both mutation and damage in selected systems. They have little power to assign a single primary historical selective cause.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Across taxa, compare the evolution and strength of regulative development with historical mutation load and injury exposure, and test whether correction mechanisms preferentially buffer genetic versus injury-induced deviations.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Cross-taxon measures of anatomical homeostasis are sparse.", "Mutation and damage correction often use the same mechanisms.", "Primary evolutionary reason is difficult to infer from extant data.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.64"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/levin-2022-tame-30--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/levin-2022-tame-30--gpt--dataset-2>;
